                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "aafacdc9-89b8-45c5-ac41-a12bdb4ede19",
                        "entry_id": "3fbc2a21-24a0-3fc9-9bb2-f30f5bf76bcf",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "cadavériques"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "12929394-a37d-3126-afae-668d47d4f900",
                        "entry_id": "3fbc2a21-24a0-3fc9-9bb2-f30f5bf76bcf",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Relatif à un cadavre."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "54b4dd3e-7689-4220-bf88-025a10d119d9",
                                "sense_id": "12929394-a37d-3126-afae-668d47d4f900",
                                "text": "Autopsie cadavérique."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "707818ac-9382-392e-a508-94978fc1b22d",
                        "entry_id": "3fbc2a21-24a0-3fc9-9bb2-f30f5bf76bcf",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qui a l’aspect d’un cadavre."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "broadly"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "cc4b39f9-0327-4641-a6fa-3ccb2e2c42dd",
                                "sense_id": "707818ac-9382-392e-a508-94978fc1b22d",
                                "text": "Elle avait brûlé deux cierges bénits, […], lorsqu’enfin le flux glaireux et nauséabond s'alentit, l'odeur fade devint moins pénétrante, plus lentement, le petit visage quitta son masque cadavérique."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "af7f1e8a-a0d8-41c3-953e-5e3d87c8344d",
                                "sense_id": "707818ac-9382-392e-a508-94978fc1b22d",
                                "text": "Quand Zéré entra, seuls étaient visibles chez Ouroz les trous des orbites aussi profondes, aussi creuses que dans un crâne de squelette et l’arête cadavérique du nez."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "27d32cd2-b540-4944-adff-f69d8ed05e7b",
                                "sense_id": "707818ac-9382-392e-a508-94978fc1b22d",
                                "text": "Mais c’est cadavérique, cette ambiance de pète sec."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "cedfec34-7638-4f23-b7e1-f0080efd8327",
                        "source_entry_id": "3fbc2a21-24a0-3fc9-9bb2-f30f5bf76bcf",
                        "target_lang_word": "cadaveric",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "cadaveric",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "50bd3c56-1b6a-3283-90a4-3d0cd8182ced",
                                        "entry_id": "6dc56a30-0d9a-3f09-bcf8-efad65a5ec77",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Pertaining to a corpse."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d0341dc8-27ce-40e2-b5e8-115a32abed6e",
                                                "sense_id": "50bd3c56-1b6a-3283-90a4-3d0cd8182ced",
                                                "text": "Hodgkin had just returned from his second visit to Paris, where he had learned to prepare and dissect cadaveric specimens."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "29b672cd-f062-3cc2-bf03-ec7421837382",
                                        "entry_id": "6dc56a30-0d9a-3f09-bcf8-efad65a5ec77",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Caused by coming into contact with a dead body, a cadaver."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ecd8e3e4-dbb8-4fbb-acc4-0ee7b689e934",
                                                "sense_id": "29b672cd-f062-3cc2-bf03-ec7421837382",
                                                "text": "He invoked cadaveric poisoning as the reason for the high death rate among priests and monks […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "36f8a8df-b734-4379-b4cc-4b339636944c",
                        "source_entry_id": "3fbc2a21-24a0-3fc9-9bb2-f30f5bf76bcf",
                        "target_lang_word": "cadaverous",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "cadaverous",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f5f4e1f4-1d86-3656-a9fc-9a2cb00af96f",
                                        "entry_id": "36cef88e-f22f-3afc-8144-dc0f746c0801",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Corpselike; hinting of death; imitating a cadaver."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9f2f8d94-9765-4068-af0e-83a95c43fb55",
                                                "sense_id": "f5f4e1f4-1d86-3656-a9fc-9a2cb00af96f",
                                                "text": "The speakers were three men, rather beyond middle life. One was pale and cadaverous, as if every feature gave testimony to the length of his vigils and the rigour of his fasts, while straight black hair hanging down on each side his face added to his wild and neglected appearance."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4d117f61-a7f2-4250-9481-ac4c67cbf7d8",
                                                "sense_id": "f5f4e1f4-1d86-3656-a9fc-9a2cb00af96f",
                                                "text": "It may have been the sight of that cadaverous ambition and self-complacent meanness, which showed itself in Paley’s yellow face, and twinkled in his narrow eyes, or it may have been a natural appetite for pleasure and joviality, of which it must be confessed Mr. Pen was exceedingly fond, which deterred that luckless youth from pursuing his designs upon the Bench or the Woolsack with the ardour, or rather steadiness, which is requisite in gentlemen who would climb to those seats of honour."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c48396fc-fb41-4495-bef5-1a32f2927d35",
                                                "sense_id": "f5f4e1f4-1d86-3656-a9fc-9a2cb00af96f",
                                                "text": "Some approached pure blanching; some had a bluish pallor; some worn by the older characters (which had possibly lain by folded for many a year) inclined to a cadaverous tint, and to a Georgian style."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9ceec39f-484a-4fb6-9283-71e0f8b5ae00",
                                                "sense_id": "f5f4e1f4-1d86-3656-a9fc-9a2cb00af96f",
                                                "text": "1917 rev. 1925 Ezra Pound, \"Canto I\"\nDark blood flowed in the fosse,\nSouls out of Erebus, cadaverous dead ..."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b573a109-76d8-48ac-a921-adead6744151",
                                                "sense_id": "f5f4e1f4-1d86-3656-a9fc-9a2cb00af96f",
                                                "text": "By some paradoxical evolution rancour and intolerance have been established in the vanguard of primitive Christianity. Mrs. Spoker, in common with many of the stricter disciples of righteousness, was as inclement in demeanour as she was cadaverous in aspect."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
